From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm: per-plane color management through msm plane color pipelines

The msm DPU can expose a per-plane color pipeline of a 257-entry 1D LUT
followed by a 17^3 3D LUT, the same shape as gamescope's per-EOTF shaper
and 3D LUT. When the planes offer it, each directly scanned-out layer
gets the tables of its own EOTF, so an HDR10 game with SDR overlays on a
gamma 2.2 HDR panel no longer needs composition, and the post-blend
output LUTs are not used. libliftoff cannot place the per-plane colorop
properties, so they are added after it picks the planes and the finished
request is tested once more; a failure composites as before. scRGB,
YCbCr and layers with a CTM still composite. The client cap hides the
legacy plane color properties, so it is only requested on msm.
---
